WEBVTT

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.600
Y-You were alive... Gucchi!

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.430
You okay, Chuta?

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:17.360
Gucchi?

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.610
I haven't forgotten...

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.070
The fact that you 
made us fall off a cliff...

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.880
Gucchi, Michiyo, Matsutaro.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.760
Since we're on this field trip, 
let's climb to the top of Mount Taketori.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:34.400
Okay.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.760
That sounds fun!

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.270
I wonder if it's really okay for us 
to go off on our own like this.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:39.590
It'll be fine!

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.640
We should enjoy our free time.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:45.910
It'll be fine!

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:48.510
There's a lot of time before we 
have to meet back up with everyone.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:51.210
Are you talking to yourself again, Chuta?

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.650
Oh, sorry.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.400
Gucchi! Michiyo! Matsutaro!

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.100
Help me!

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.390
I'm scared!

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.900
Wait right there! I'll save you!

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.410
Okay... Huh? What?

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.200
The right? Got it!

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.320
<b>A Pursuer From the Past: Part 2</b>

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:57.570
It's true that we were in a
 dangerous situation back then,

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:01.390
but we should have just stayed 
on that ledge and waited for help.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:06.930
If only a certain someone hadn't 
destroyed a precarious ledge...

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.330
Calm your breathing, Chuta.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.810
<i>Calm down... Calm down... Say it now.</i>

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.540
<i>Say what you've been waiting 
to say all this time.</i>

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.620
I'm sorry, Gucchi...

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:21.780
Huh?

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.720
You know damn well sorry's not enough!

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.210
Do you know the hell I went through?

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.230
After falling off the ledge,

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.060
I crashed into the ground, 
and was crushed by rocks.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.280
I heard things breaking 
all throughout my body.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:39.580
I knew I was going to die...

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:46.180
But as my conscious was fading, 
I was engulfed by light...

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:50.440
I... miraculously came back to life.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.920
Because of them.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:54.610
Them?

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:55.660
Someone's coming.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.210
That was actually quite the climb.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:02.080
Excuse me, would you take our picture?

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.580
Don't butt into our conversation.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.120
A bomb?

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.560
Chuta, look.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:16.440
No!

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.510
Wh-What are you doing, Gucchi?!

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:22.680
And what are you expecting from me?

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:26.270
I'm not the same Gucchi anymore.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:31.370
DeMille's mark... Are you...

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:36.830
Yeah. DeMille saved my life, 
so I joined them.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.740
I'm currently a captain that's 
in charge of his own vessel.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.790
Y-You're lying...

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:44.720
My mission is to analyze the forces

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.010
that stand in the way of 
DeMille's plan to take over Earth.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:50.600
Which means the analysis 
of ēlDLIVE's power.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:54.930
I knew that ēlDLIVE personnel 
were hiding in Shirobori Middle School,

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:57.550
but I hadn't been able to 
pinpoint who they were.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.770
So I sent in my subordinates,

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:03.320
and had them smoke out the personnel 
by using the sleeping SPH.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.790
So that was SPH...

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.840
DeMille was behind that after all!

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.670
But I must say that I was surprised.

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:11.720
To think that you'd be in ēlDLIVE...

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:16.240
And you have graciously helped me
 accomplish my second mission.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:17.830
Second mission?

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:20.940
It's to steal your Monitalien.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:23.040
What?! Steal Dolugh?!

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:26.400
Ah, so that's him.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:29.260
The value of the unknown 
technology from Planet Griffith

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:32.850
that's within that Monitalien 
is immeasurable.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:34.930
It's impossible for you to steal him!

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:36.770
There's no way for you to pull him out!

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.850
Only as long as you don't die, Chuta.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:42.530
Killing Chuta to separate 
you two won't be happening.

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:46.070
Even if the Monitalien matures, 
if its host dies,

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.820
everything other than its 
informational data gets reset.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:55.950
But with DeMille's technology, 
I can separate you while you're alive.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.050
Wha...

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.950
I don't wanna get cut.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.950
I don't wanna get hurt, either!

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:02.170
Hey.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:02.820
Roger.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:03.650
Captain.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.880
Sonokata! Inspector Chips!

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.050
Considering that we're old friends,

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.480
if you hand over the Monitalian 
without resisting,

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.500
not only will I return 
these hostages to you,

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:16.600
I'll even forget about the fact 
that you threw me off a cliff.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:17.750
Huh?!

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:20.140
I know your personality pretty well, Chuta.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:23.430
You've been blaming yourself 
ever since, haven't you?

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.670
Even though I'm the victim here,

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:28.710
I'm telling you that I'm willing 
to completely let it go.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:31.020
No one will blame you anymore.

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:33.490
You won't have to suffer.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.890
<i>I won't have to suffer...</i>

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:42.020
Chuta! I'm starting to fade.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:44.920
If that's what it'll take 
for you to forgive me...

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:45.910
Chuta?!

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:50.730
If I can forget it all...

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:52.380
Chuta!

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:57.890
You just have to give up the Monitalien 
and ask for your past to be erased.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.390
You'll feel better.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:03.990
I'll feel better...

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:06.520
Chuta, I want to continue existing with you.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:07.480
Shut up...

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:12.890
If I just hand you over, everything 
that's happened up until now...

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:14.750
All the hardships I went through...

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:17.540
All of it... All of it...

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.700
Chuta.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:21.460
All of it... All of it...

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:26.980
It looks like you've made up your mind.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:27.960
Yeah.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.490
The past doesn't need to be erased.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.450
Because...

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:38.340
...there are precious memories there, too.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.820
And... if I'm with Dolugh,

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:47.570
I can fight bad guys like you.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:48.520
So...

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:50.190
I'm not handing Dolugh over!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.200
I thank you, Gucchi.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.450
If I hadn't been reunited with you,

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:00.580
I wouldn't have ever been 
able to think like this.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:01.990
What?

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:04.390
And sorry...

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:07.920
I'm a member of the Space Police.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:10.190
You bastard...

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:13.260
Let the hostages go and give yourself up.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:16.210
Don't you move! I'll kill her!

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.370
Dolugh, can you beat that guy 
without hurting Sonokata?

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:22.820
It'd be hard at this distance.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:25.830
Wait, Chuta. Look at Misuzu's pocket!

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:29.730
A red wrapper?

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:30.670
That's...

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:35.100
That's the anti-sleep SPH waking medicine.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:42.410
You have the right to remain silent.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:46.250
Anything you say can and will be used 
against you in an intergalactic court of law.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.630
And... in the detention center,

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:52.630
you can pick a Japanese-style 
or Western-style dinner menu!

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.870
What are you talking about?

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:58.380
<i>You remember, right, Sonokata?</i>

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:01.250
By the way, the Western style is steak,

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:02.260
and the Japanese style is...

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:04.510
...salmon!

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:13.400
Please disappear without leaving a trace.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.780
SPH D Blade.

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:30.790
Huh?!

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:36.340
He's good...

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:04.330
He's on par with Misuzu.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.230
I can be, too..

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:07.570
You're in the way. Please step back!

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:09.790
She's right.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:13.540
Nothing good happens when you get involved!

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.880
Sonokata!

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:29.440
Back then...

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.850
Us falling off that cliff,

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:34.600
and this woman dying here right now,

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.390
is all your fault, Chuta!

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:45.700
Gucchi, no!

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:49.580
It's too late!

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:50.400
No!

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:51.870
Gucchi, don't!

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:55.540
This is the end!

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:58.500
Stop!

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:00.670
Sympathy!

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:24.030
<b>Chips O'Toole</b>

00:11:36.850 --> 00:11:40.180
You really haven't changed, Chuta...

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:42.840
You can never leave your friends alone.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.860
G-Gucchi!

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:47.490
Now we can finally talk.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:54.060
There was a recorder implanted here 
that DeMille uses to monitor their personnel.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.390
Huh?

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:58.280
You even took care of my subordinates,

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:01.200
so I'm not being monitored 
by anyone right now.

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:06.020
Don't worry, Chuta. 
They're not dead, either.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:07.280
Huh?

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:12.240
They're just covered in a black film 
and unconscious.

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:15.280
That's my specialty, which DeMille 
hasn't caught onto yet.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.900
Which means...

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:23.160
When you declined the deal earlier,

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:25.990
I'm not sure why, 
but it made me really happy.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:31.640
It was like, yeah... that's my buddy, Chuta.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:34.430
Gucchi... You're actually Gucchi!

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:36.350
You guys sure are buddy-buddy 
all of a sudden.

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:38.010
Wha— Shut up, Dolugh!

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:42.810
So when you were talking to yourself, 
you were actually talking to that Monitalien?

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:45.910
Yeah, I just found that out recently.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.570
It's not that funny.

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:51.210
There's something that I'm 
pretty certain about.

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:51.780
Hm?

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:55.540
Michiyo and Matsutaro are alive 
somewhere in the universe.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.490
Huh? Really?!

00:12:57.490 --> 00:13:00.940
For sure! Even I was alive.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:05.640
Also... I plan to stay in DeMille 
a little longer.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.210
I'll use DeMille,

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:10.760
and you use ēlDLIVE to 
find Michiyo and Matsutaro.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:14.040
I see... Yeah, that's a great idea!

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:16.060
Right? Ow...

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:16.690
Are you okay?

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:18.400
It hurts.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.770
Sorry... It's all because of me again.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:24.150
That was an unavoidable accident.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:28.860
The part of the cliff we were on 
was already starting to crumble.

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:37.020
But knowing you, I figured you'd been 
blaming yourself this whole time...

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:38.830
And I was exactly right.

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:40.750
Gucchi...

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:45.210
Sonokata!

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:46.500
You're in the way.

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:51.920
Don't tell anyone what we talked about.

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:53.670
It's better off if we seem like enemies.

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:57.720
Gucchi, if you fail your mission, 
aren't you going to get killed?

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:00.240
I'm not like the grunts.

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:01.860
They won't get rid of me that easily.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.890
More importantly, you should be 
worrying about your own ship.

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:06.880
I'm not gonna hold back!

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:10.000
Also... don't worry about my mom.

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:12.820
I'm surprised you're still alive,

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:14.740
though you were in the way.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.200
S-Sorry...

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:20.430
Chuta! The Solar System Bureau is in danger!

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:23.240
Oh, yeah. Sonokata! DeMille...

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:31.420
These fireworks are the way you guys 
communicate when you can't use the radio?

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:36.460
It stinks! It stinks! It stinks! It stinks!

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:36.460
We shoot up the cartridge SPH 
in order as a sign.

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:38.450
How's the analysis on the jamming going?

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:40.090
It's complete!

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:44.440
Chief! I've detected an emergency signal
 from the Earth 34th Local Branch.

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:45.760
It must be Misuzu and the others!

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.440
I'm gonna read it.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.540
"There is a strong possibility that DeMille 
will attack the bureau directly."

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:51.450
Understood.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.780
All units, prepare for battle.

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:57.950
Room Chief Magnoli, hurry and 
generate the SPH barrier.

00:14:57.950 --> 00:14:59.060
Yoyosa!

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:00.800
What's wrong?

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:02.420
There's been an explosion nearby.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:03.500
Harry!

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:07.210
The jamming nullification wave
 is ready to go. Firing!

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:09.500
Bringing the radar back online.

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.800
We're being surrounded 
by multiple small-scale mines.

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.380
What?

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:16.630
Shoot them down!

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:17.470
Yoyosa!

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:25.390
This is the traffic division. 
We've got a gaping hole!

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:26.200
How's the engine?

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:26.940
It's intact!

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:31.160
They're so fast that we 
can't hit them with the lasers.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.060
What's the status on the SPH barrier?

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:34.550
Good to go, ribbit!

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:35.690
Do it!

00:15:35.690 --> 00:15:41.230
All right, space moss. Make sure you 
spit out plenty of barrier SPH, ribbit.

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:47.840
Protection SPH spraying.

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:49.760
Ow!

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:51.450
Welcome back, shero.

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:52.580
Can we get a status report?

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:55.230
We're being attacked by multiple 
small-scale mines, shero.

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:01.360
It's better off if we seem like enemies. {lit for both instances of this line: We're better off as enemies}

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:04.600
<i>Yeah, but do you have to go this far?</i>

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:05.580
It's no use!

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:07.220
There're just too many mines!

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:11.600
What are you gonna do, ēlDLIVE Captain?

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:13.960
What's wrong, Chuta?

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:16.860
I was just thinking those small-scale 
mines looked like something...

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:19.590
You mean our battle training?

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:21.580
Yeah, that!

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:23.520
Chief Laine!

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.780
Hey. You're alive.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:28.070
I have an idea!

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:32.210
You think up some interesting things.

00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:35.740
I remembered the training 
from the other day.

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:39.600
I'm sure that Tonto-san's fly-swatting 
will be able to defeat those mines!

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:42.760
I'll give it a shot. 
Chief, I'm about to begin.

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:43.850
Thanks.

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:48.320
The connection between all the gun ports 
and my paw pads is complete.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.330
Aligning hologram deployed!

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:53.530
This ship is now my body...

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:56.270
...and the laser cannons are my paw pads!

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:58.630
There, meow!

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:09.590
Wow, not bad. Then...

00:17:13.610 --> 00:17:15.460
They moved to where the lasers won't reach.

00:17:15.460 --> 00:17:17.340
This is the laser cannon pod.

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:19.860
Please turn the bow of the ship 
60 degrees to the left.

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:22.420
Port! Turning the bow of 
the ship 60 degrees...

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:24.550
Wait. Keep the angle as-is.

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:25.600
But...

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:29.380
Fire the elmaser cannons! 
Spread it out as wide as possible.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:30.270
Yoyosa!

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:33.420
Harry! From the sector which is 
30 degrees from starboard,

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:37.950
analyze the optimal position 
to blanket Japan with SPH,

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.520
and target that point.

00:17:39.520 --> 00:17:42.690
But I don't see anything at the target...

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:47.310
It doesn't matter. Fire the elmaser cannons!

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:56.720
That's...

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.040
...a DeMille ship!

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:00.040
Lucky us.

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:03.790
I see. So the enemy was 
intentionally trying to get

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:06.900
the <i>Jeanrenoi-R</i> to 
face left by using the mines.

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:09.530
By facing to the side and 
exposing more surface area,

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:12.150
they would have been able to shoot their
 main armament directly at the ship's body.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:16.020
That's how the chief knew that the enemy ship 
was 30 degrees from starboard.

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:21.710
We also found a hint from their new weapon 
that was blocking the SPH radar.

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:25.490
The enemy vessel was located at the 
most optimal SPH firing point.

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:29.840
I'm not really sure I understand, 
but the chief must be amazing.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.780
Our stealth dome has been eliminated.

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:34.460
We're in plain sight.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:38.750
Yeah, apparently that ship's captain 
has been in a few battles.

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:40.690
I guess we should fall back.

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:42.800
Huh? What about our counterattack?

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:45.590
We got the data we were after.

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:48.840
<i>You found yourself a good bureau, Chuta.</i>

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:50.790
<i>See you soon!</i>

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:55.810
The DeMille vessel is 
about enter warp speed.

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:57.290
They've disappeared from our radars.

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:58.650
The mines have also stopped functioning.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:02.150
It looks like the DeMille ship 
was able to get away for now.

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:03.030
Yeah.

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:11.010
Jeez... You scared me for a sec, Gucchi...

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:26.890
<b>Mizoguchi Family Grave</b>

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:22.010
I was lucky because of Gucchi.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:22.900
Huh?

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:25.380
You said we could coexist.

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:26.880
You consider that lucky?

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:28.420
Is it not?

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:30.450
I guess it wouldn't be unlucky...

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:34.590
<i>Honestly, back there, somehow...</i>

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:37.810
<i>I felt courage welling up inside me 
when I looked into Dolugh's eyes.</i>

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:41.700
<b>Mizoguchi Family Grave</b>

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:40.220
Chuta Kokonose-kun, right?

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:44.780
Gucchi's mom...

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:49.030
It's been a while. Um, I'll be going now.

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:52.740
Please wait, Chuta-kun.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:59.960
Please forgive me 
for blaming you back then...

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:02.540
I was wrong.

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:04.590
I'm very sorry.

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:05.860
Huh?

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:10.480
A month before the field trip 
when Ken came home covered in dirt...

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:12.890
My friends gave me these.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:16.850
...he was so happy as he held that blue box..

00:20:16.850 --> 00:20:20.190
It must have been the time capsule 
we all put together.

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:25.740
So Gucchi actually dug it up and 
brought it home right after...

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:28.310
That was why we couldn't find it.

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:31.150
It was in Ken's room this whole time,

00:20:31.150 --> 00:20:34.210
but yesterday, I heard something, 
so I went to check...

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:37.920
It had disappeared suddenly.

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:44.220
And this was there instead.

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:49.640
There's no reason this badge 
should be in our house.

00:20:50.070 --> 00:20:54.060
Because it was on his backpack 
the day he disappeared...

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:58.760
He's alive...

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:02.690
He's holding the fun memories 
he had with all of you close.

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:08.980
<i>I want to tell her that I met Gucchi, but...</i>

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:10.650
Chuta-kun.

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:16.830
If he came back, 
would you play with him again?

00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:18.890
Yes.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:22.720
To think that the captain 
of the DeMille vessel

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:25.430
was a childhood friend 
of Officer Kokonose...

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:30.360
But why is his picture 
in this old case file?

00:21:30.360 --> 00:21:33.010
About that... Actually...

00:21:33.010 --> 00:21:35.260
Chief! We have a visitor from HQ.

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:37.320
I'm coming in.

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:45.470
I am Belalugo, a high-ranking investigator 
working directly under Mothers.

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:52.350
Chuta, this is your chance to learn 
how to write up a report.

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:56.540
I'm sure she's just going to mock me, like,
 "You can't even write up reports?" as usual.

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:05.080
By the way, I've been meaning to ask...

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:09.250
You were faking being asleep 
and being taken hostage,

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:11.400
so why didn't you wake up earlier?

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:14.250
So they'd lead me to the ship's captain.

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:15.560
I see.

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:21.320
And if you had succumbed to the enemy's
 psychological attack and agreed to the deal,

00:22:21.320 --> 00:22:22.830
you would have been 
deemed unfit for this job,

00:22:22.830 --> 00:22:25.690
and I could have had you kicked out 
of ēlDLIVE without a trace.

00:22:25.690 --> 00:22:28.670
Huh?! So you were testing me?

00:22:29.220 --> 00:22:35.490
But... you made the right decision. 
I actually see you in a new light, slightly.

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:38.380
There you go, bringing me down....

00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:40.660
Huh? What did you just...

00:22:41.400 --> 00:22:43.210
I said that I see you in a new light.

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:45.100
What?! No way!

00:22:45.100 --> 00:22:47.140
That's the first time 
Misuzu's complimented you.

00:22:47.650 --> 00:22:49.770
May I continue eating now?

00:22:49.770 --> 00:22:52.970
Sonokata... you got something...

00:22:57.990 --> 00:22:59.970
S-Stop laughing at me.

00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:05.270
<i>Maybe... I've been wrong about Sonokata.</i>

00:23:05.270 --> 00:23:06.020
Chuta!

00:23:09.160 --> 00:23:11.900
Freeze, Misuzu Sonokata!

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:17.620
You're under arrest on suspicion 
of aiding and abetting of a murderer.

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:21.330
Huh? Sonokata's being arrested?

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:27.510
This salmon bento is really good.

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:28.590
Really?

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:31.120
I heard that sake lees 
are good for your skin, too.

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:34.630
Officer Kokonose, please stop 
saying "sake" so carelessly.

00:23:34.630 --> 00:23:35.970
Next time on <i>ēlDLIVE,</i>

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Next Time
Something to Believe in: Part 1</b>

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.140
"Something to Believe in: Part 1."

00:23:38.140 --> 00:23:39.550
That's absurd!
